" **Supplier Terms and Conditions - Nordhaven Marine Supply AS**\n\n1. **Introduction**\n\nThese Supplier Terms and Conditions govern the relationship between Nordhaven Marine Supply AS (hereinafter referred to as \"Nordhaven\") and the Client. By placing an order, the Client accepts these terms in their entirety.\n\n2. **Stocked Items**\n   - Standard lead time for delivery of stocked items is 3-5 business days from the date of order confirmation.\n   - Made-to-Order Items:\n     - Standard lead time is 4-6 weeks from the date of order confirmation.\n     - Custom orders may require additional lead time, as communicated by Nordhaven at the time of order placement.\n\n3. **Minimum Order Value**\n   - The minimum order value for standard purchases is \u20ac1000 excluding VAT and shipping costs.\n\n4. **Payment Terms**\n   - Payments are due within 30 days from the invoice date.\n   - Early-payment discount of 2% is applicable if payment is received within 7 days from the invoice date.\n\n5. **Warranty and Returns**\n   - Nordhaven offers a warranty of 12 months on all parts against defects in materials and workmanship.\n   - Return requests must be submitted within 14 days of delivery, and returned items must be unopened and in their original packaging.\n   - A restocking fee of 15% may apply to returns, at Nordhaven's discretion.\n\n6. **Freight Terms (Incoterms)**\n   - All orders are delivered DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) to the Client's specified address. This includes all freight costs, customs duties, and taxes.\n\n7. **Expedited Shipping**\n   - For expedited shipping, an additional 15% surcharge will apply to the total order value.\n\n8. **Contact Information for Urgent Orders**\n   - For urgent orders or inquiries outside of regular business hours, please email urgency@nordhavensupply.com.\n\n9. **General Provisions**\n   - Any amendments to these terms must be agreed upon in writing by both parties.\n   - In case of any discrepancies between languages, the English version shall prevail.\n   - These terms are governed by and construed in accordance with Norwegian law.\n\n10. **Force Majeure**\n    - Nordhaven shall not be liable for any failure or delay in performance of its obligations under these terms where such failure or delay results from events beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, governmental actions, wars, terrorist activities, and labor disputes."